The core allegation in that report is that compliance reports may have been auto-generated from templates without
      genuine independent audit procedures. These are serious allegations, but they remain allegations. We donotguarantee the
      accuracy, completeness, or currentness of any data on this page. Company names, audit dates, and other details were
      extracted programmatically from the archived spreadsheet and may contain errors introduced during collection or processing. The purpose of this database is not to accuse or single out any individual company. That said, the publicly available evidence
      is concerning enough that organizations listed here, along with their clients, partners, or regulators, may
      want to independently verify the validity of any SOC 2 or ISO 27001 reports obtained through the platform in question.
      Relying parties are encouraged to request the original auditor's attestation letter and to confirm the auditor's
      independence and standing with the relevant professional body. Applicable regulatory frameworks:AICPA Code of Professional Conduct §§ 1.200, 1.295 (auditor independence);
        AT-C Section 205 (examination engagements);
        AT-C Section 320 (reporting on an examination of controls at a service organization, i.e. SOC 2);
        ISO/IEC 17021-1:2015 (requirements for certification audit bodies);
        HIPAA (45 CFR §§ 160–164, criminal penalties for knowingly misrepresenting compliance);
        GDPR Art. 5(2), Art. 24, Art. 83 (controller accountability and administrative fines up to €20M or 4% of global annual turnover);
